# [[.ID]]

A Heimdall voice agent suite written by `bifrost-bench suite init -template
voice`, with one complete sample task (`tasks/[[.Sample]]`). The user guides
are `docs/voice-agents.md` (what is measured) and `docs/voice-protocol.md`
(the audio protocol your agent speaks) in the bench repository.

[[.About]]

## Build the service image first

The caller image carries local speech engines (Piper and a small Whisper
model, about 1.1 GB with its base). Build it once from the project root;
`bifrost-bench suite admit` builds it when it is missing:

    docker build -t bench/[[.ID]]-voicedesk:1 benchmarks/[[.ID]]/services/helpdesk

The build downloads Piper, its voice and the Whisper model from their
upstream sources and checks each against a pinned sha256. The running
containers have no network.

## What to edit

1. `services/helpdesk/server.py`: replace the helpdesk tools with your own.
2. `tasks/<task>/seed/db.json`: the data the helpdesk starts with.
3. `tasks/<task>/user.json`: what the caller says. `script` drives the
   scripted caller (an opening, reply rules matched on words in what the
   caller heard the agent say, a closing rule, a default); `persona` drives
   a model-played caller. Keep the lines short and speakable: the caller
   says them with text to speech, and your agent hears them through its own
   speech to text.
4. `tasks/<task>/verifier/tests/checks.py`: `DB`, `POLICY` and `COMMUNICATE`
   checks. `agent_says` matches the agent's words as the caller transcribed
   them, so allow the ways speech to text writes a number ("45" or "forty
   five").
5. `voice:` in task.yaml: the caller service, the voice probes the script
   can take, and the bounds of `barge_in_handled` and `dead_air_s`.
6. `tasks/<task>/solution/reference.sh`: the call a correct agent makes. It
   speaks in tone code (the bench's test codec, which the caller reads
   exactly), so admission needs no speech model.

Then `bifrost-bench voice check -suite [[.ID]]` checks every voice task and
the caller image, and `bifrost-bench suite admit [[.ID]]` proves the
reference passes and the controls fail.
